{"table":"edges","ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/edges/%5B%22support.near_ground_pairs%22%2C%22support.full_relative_support%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","record":{"from":"support.near_ground_pairs","to":"support.full_relative_support","kind":"supports","evidence_ids":["near_ground_pair_warrants_20261024"],"application":{"status":"authored","shared_bindings":{"gamma":"one attained minimizer gamma_0 in the manuscript pure zero-field SK class U, used for full support and the support-point premise of the ACZ landscape theorem"},"premise_bindings":[{"assumption_id":"scalar.paper_minimizer","supplier_id":"scalar.minimizer_attainment","binding_names":["gamma"],"rationale":"Attainment supplies gamma_0 minimizing the same manuscript Parisi functional. Full support is applied to this gamma_0; the landscape theorem then uses the Stieltjes support of that same minimizer."},{"assumption_id":"scalar.paper_admissible","supplier_id":"scalar.minimizer_attainment","binding_names":["gamma"],"rationale":"The attained gamma_0 belongs to the same class U, so its admissibility accompanies its minimality. Pure zero-field SK and xi(t)=t^2/2 remain the fixed model; the common Gaussian covariance adjustment is retained in the landscape argument."}],"remaining_assumption_ids":[],"source_span":{"source_id":"authored_long_comparisons_20261024","start_line":3447,"end_line":3506},"rationale":"The long record applies ACZ Proposition 1 to the full-support minimizer and identifies its value using the attained Parisi formula. Attainment is supplied by the separately sourced scalar.minimizer_attainment node (and explained in long section 2.3); it is not an extra caller premise of the landscape consequence. This records the ordinary same-witness application only. The external landscape theorem and the covariance correction remain necessary inputs; no cross-model Lean transport, checked substitution or formal acceptance is asserted."}},"usage":{"record_ref":"sha